WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.330
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Welcome
to Deconstructing Chatbots.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.800
I am Priyanka Vergadia,
and in today's episode,

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:08.060
we are going to explore
how to integrate Dialogflow

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.230
with Telephony Gateway.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.632
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.190
The other day, I was talking
to a friend about chatbots.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.380
And he said, Priyanka,
it would really

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.470
help me if I could just assign
a phone number to the chatbot

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.020
that I already have
built. That way

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:29.420
I can provide the same
experience to my users

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.550
across the phone and web.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.600
Well, that led me
to this episode.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.010
So today, we are going to
work with the same appointment

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.220
scheduler chatbot that we
built in the previous episodes

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.740
and integrate it with
the Telephony Gateway

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.780
so our users
calling on the phone

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.230
can get the same experience
as the ones on the web.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.650
Now, remember that this
is a feature in beta

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.860
so you may want to let us know
how you're using it so that we

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.440
can keep improving it.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.570
Let's get in our
Dialogflow console

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:02.300
and locate our agent,
Appointment Scheduler,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.900
with our intents.

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:06.390
We are going to go into
integration section

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:09.860
where we enabled our web
and Google Home integration.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:13.100
This time we will select
Dialogflow Phone Gateway.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.430
It allows you to select the
country for the phone number.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.210
And in next step, you
choose the phone number.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.830
I'm good with the
default selection,

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:24.430
and we'll just finish it here.

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.250
Once you finish, you'll see
the Congratulations message

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.410
indicating a phone
number that's assigned

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:32.290
to your bot for your
users to call in.

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.080
Now as you can see in yellow,
the phone number you get

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.848
is valid only for 30 days if
you're using Standard Edition.

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:40.390
If you are a business,
you definitely

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:41.560
want a permanent number.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:45.010
So for that, you should be
using Enterprise Edition.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.690
Let's place a call to our
bot at 267-281-5159, which

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.000
is the number that we assigned.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:52.690
CHATBOT: Hello.

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:53.610
How can I help you?

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.360
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Schedule an appointment

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:56.770
for 4:00 PM tomorrow.

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.810
CHATBOT: What services
are you looking to get?

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:02.740
DMV offers driver license and
vehicle registration services.

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.290
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
Driver's license.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.373
CHATBOT: You are all set
for your driver's license

00:02:06.373 --> 00:02:10.419
on the 25th of January 2019
at 16 hours zero minutes

00:02:10.419 --> 00:02:11.530
and zero seconds.

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:12.072
See you then.

00:02:12.072 --> 00:02:13.280
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: All right.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.060
So my friend is really
happy now that he can just

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.100
assign a phone
number to his chatbot

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.330
and provide the same experience
across web and phone channels.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:25.000
Don't miss the next episode
of Deconstructing Chatbots

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.480
because we are going to
learn more about entities.

